- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Egypt: Freedom in the World 2023 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/egypt/freedom-world/2023","claim":"The report says Sisi governed Egypt in an increasingly authoritarian manner, that meaningful political opposition was virtually nonexistent, and that dissent, press freedom, and assembly were tightly restricted; it also notes ANHRI suspended Egyptian operations in January 2022 after years of harassment.","locator":"Overview and Key Developments in 2022","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Annual country report with explicit 2022 summary and detailed political-rights sections.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"retrospective coverage of target-year 2022","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Sisi and his government rather than to a generic country baseline.","contrary_evidence":["The report is retrospective and aggregates multiple episodes rather than isolating each 2022 decision."],"lenses":["4B.1","4B.3","4B.6","4B.9","4B.10"]}
- SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Egypt: Freedom in the World 2023 Country Report","publisher":"Freedom House","publication_date":"2023","url":"https://freedomhouse.org/country/egypt/freedom-world/2023","claim":"In July 2022 Sisi appointed a military general to the Supreme Constitutional Court's first deputy justice post, and the report says the 2018 election was unfair and noncompetitive, with state resources and media used to support Sisi and opposition candidates pressured to withdraw.","locator":"A1, A3, and F1 sections","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Specific 2022 court-appointment detail plus election analysis in the same annual report.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 institutional-capture and election-quality context","ruler_attribution":"Directly tied to Sisi's appointment power and regime entrenchment choices.","contrary_evidence":["The report notes the state of emergency was suspended in 2021, but says repressive legislation remained in place."],"lenses":["4B.2","4B.4","4B.5","4B.8","4B.10"]}
